target/
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk
.claude/worktrees/

# Machine-local cargo settings, chiefly a shared `build.target-dir`.
#
# Deliberately untracked rather than committed. Cargo resolves a relative
# `target-dir` against the directory holding the config file, and it discovers
# config by walking *up* from the current directory — so a tracked
# `.cargo/config.toml` would appear inside every git worktree and each one would
# resolve to its own `target/`, which is the opposite of sharing. Only an
# untracked file at the repo root is found from every worktree and points them
# all at the same absolute path.
#
# The cost of not sharing is not theoretical: five worktrees each rebuilt
# whisper.cpp from source, 7.5 GB of `whisper-rs-sys` artifacts across 39 GB of
# `target/` directories.
.cargo/

# Spikes are throwaway probes that answer a question and are kept only as
# executable evidence for docs/spikes/. Their lockfiles pin heavy native
# dependencies (whisper.cpp, ONNX Runtime) that are not workspace dependencies.
spikes/*/Cargo.lock

# Reproducible extract of govox-py at the commit named in REFERENCE. Derived,
# never edited, and re-created on demand by tools/parity-gen/pinned-source.sh.
tools/parity-gen/.parity-src/
